          "reasoning_content": "We need to extract unverified occupational, executive, ownership, founder, board or trustee role proposals.\n\nFrom entries:\n\nEntry0: \"Inez Rao met Paolo Wu at Tamarack Power.\" No role claim; just meeting location. No role proposals.\n\nEntry1: \"The notice names Inez Rao as secretary of Ash Works; it gives no employer or role for Paolo Wu.\"\n\nThis claims Inez Rao is secretary of Ash Works. Secretary is a role. Need to assess taxonomy: executive, board_director, controlling_owner, employee, founder, owner, unknown. \"Secretary\" could be an employee role, possibly corporate officer. It's an executive role? Usually corporate secretary is an officer, but taxonomy includes executive. The rule: Use unknown if not supported. Generic \"secretary\" may not indicate executive scope, but could be employee. The taxonomy has employee. So we can map to role_kind = employee (or executive?). The instruction: \"A generic director or secretary title alone does not establish board or executive scope.\" So not executive. So role_kind = employee.\n\nThus we have one role interpretation: Inez Rao as secretary of Ash Works.\n\nWe must create selection IDs (unique). For each role, we need a selection focusing on the role title \"secretary\". The focus selection covers the token(s) \"secretary\". In entry1 tokens: id6 is \"secretary\". So selection first_token=6 last_token=6.\n\nAlso need subject_surface selection for the name \"Inez Rao\". Could be tokens 3-4? In entry1, token ids 3 \"Inez\", 4 \"Rao\". So selection subject surface tokens 3-4.\n\nOrganization_surface selection for \"Ash Works\": tokens 8-9? token 8 \"Ash\", token9 \"Works\". So selection organization tokens 8-9.\n\nNow interpretations:\n\nid say \"i0\"? Use unique id.\n\nInterpretation fields: id, statement_entry (entry 1), focus (selection id), kind \"role\", normalized short label e.g., \"secretary\". role_kind \"employee\". subjects list candidate mention IDs: candidate person IDs